e (79). Leesburg's all-time high is 101\u00b0F, on August 13, 1991.","t_chg":"Leesburg's days and nights both warmed. Nights warmed faster.","p_chg":"Across 63 complete years: Leesburg's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.77\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.62 to +0.93), about +5.1\u00b0F since 1959. Leesburg's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.29\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.14 to +0.44), about +1.9\u00b0F since 1959.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 11 of 12 months. Highs rose in 6 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Leesburg's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.78 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 45.1 inches a year. The wettest year was 1959 (67.58 in); the driest, 2000 (26.47 in). Leesburg almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.0 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 11 daily record highs, 3 daily record lows"}}